  "title": "The role of REM sleep in neural differentiation of memories in the hippocampus",
  "description": "This dataset contains fMRI and EEG recordings from 69 participants examining the role of rapid eye movement (REM) sleep in the neural differentiation of memories in the hippocampus. Each participant completed three fMRI scans and one EEG session, which contained either nap sleep data or quiet wake data depending on the participant's condition.",
  "methods_description": "Data collection included three fMRI scans and one EEG session per participant. The EEG session recorded either sleep (nap) or quiet wake data depending on the participant's assigned condition. Participants also completed behavioral tasks including a decision task and a reward prediction task during fMRI sessions.",
